o Warn on all-null coordinate / centroid columns in the spatial write path.
  Benchmarking surfaced a release whose x_centroid / y_centroid columns were
  100% null while the real per-cell coordinates lived in separate columns, which
  forced a downstream fallback. A coordinate or centroid column that is entirely
  null in a spatial resource is almost certainly an upstream mapping error, so
  the writer should emit a warning rather than silently persist it. The actual
  fix belongs in whatever assembles the object; this is the guard that would
  catch it at write time.
